{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets all even bits of a given number. Even bit positions are 1-indexed (2, 4, 6, ...).\"\"\"\n\n    def generateMask(upToBit: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Generates a mask with 1s at even 1-indexed bit positions up to upToBit.\"\"\"\n        mask = 0\n        for i in range(1, upToBit + 1):\n            if i % 2 == 0:\n                mask |= (1 << (i - 1))\n        return mask\n\n    upToBit = max(2, n.bit_length())\n    mask = generateMask(upToBit)\n    return n | mask"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple, Dict\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass\nclass CanonicalPair:\n    a: int\n    b: int\n\n    @classmethod\n    def normalize(cls, t: Tuple[int, int]) -> 'CanonicalPair':\n        \"\"\"Normalizes an input tuple to a CanonicalPair with a <= b.\"\"\"\n        x, y = t\n        return cls(a=min(x, y), b=max(x, y))\n\ndef check_occurences(tuples: List[Tuple[int, int]]) -> Dict[Tuple[int, int], int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts occurrences of canonicalized tuples in a list.\n    Each tuple (x, y) is canonicalized to (min(x, y), max(x, y)) before counting.\n    \"\"\"\n    result: Dict[Tuple[int, int], int] = {}\n    for t in tuples:\n        cp = CanonicalPair.normalize(t)\n        key = (cp.a, cp.b)\n        result[key] = result.get(key, 0) + 1\n    return result"}
