{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of sequences of length n with elements in [1, m],\n    where each element is at least twice the previous one.\"\"\"\n\n    # dp[k][i] stores the number of sequences of length k that start with element i.\n    # Dimensions: (n + 1) for length (0 to n), (m + 1) for starting value (0 to m).\n    dp = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: For sequences of length 1, any integer i from 1 to m is a valid sequence.\n    for i in range(1, m + 1):\n        dp[1][i] = 1\n\n    # Build up the dp table for lengths from 2 to n.\n    for k in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(1, m + 1):  # Iterate through possible starting elements 'i'\n            # The next element 'j' in the sequence must satisfy j >= 2*i and j <= m.\n            min_next_val = 2 * i\n            \n            # If 2*i exceeds m, no valid next element exists, so dp[k][i] remains 0.\n            if min_next_val > m:\n                continue\n            \n            # Sum up the counts of sequences of length (k-1) that can follow 'i'.\n            for j in range(min_next_val, m + 1):\n                dp[k][i] += dp[k-1][j]\n    \n    # The total number of sequences of length n is the sum of all dp[n][i] for i from 1 to m.\n    total_sequences = sum(dp[n][i] for i in range(1, m + 1))\n    \n    return total_sequences"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/240", "solution": "def replace_list(first_list, second_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Replaces the last element of the first list with the elements of the second list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(first_list) == 1:\n        return second_list\n    elif len(second_list) == 0:\n        return first_list[:-1]\n    else:\n        return first_list[:-1] + second_list"}
